                "notes": "identifier CHEBI:34683 -> kgmicrobe.compound:na2hpo4_x_7_h2o; mapping_quality EXACT_MATCH -> NARROW_MATCH. The record is a hydrate of CHEBI:34683 ('disodium hydrogenphosphate') and was sharing that term's identifier — the identity collapse MAPPING_SEMANTICS §3 forbids, which made a distinct substance indistinguishable from its anhydrous parent downstream. ChEBI has no term for this hydrate and the record carries no verified CAS, so steps 1 and 2 are unavailable and step 3 applies.",
                "source": "MIM curation (#321/#334)"
              },
              {
                "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
                "notes": "molecular_formula 'HO4P.2Na' -> 'HO4P.2Na.7H2O'. The recorded value described the anhydrous salt while the label names a hydrate, understating the mass by 18 g/mol per water. Corrected because the label states 7 water(s) of hydration, and the recorded formula was byte-identical to the anhydrous parent CHEBI:34683's ChEBI formula ('HO4P.2Na') — the mark of a value inherited from the parent rather than measured for this record. Water appended in ChEBI's own dot-separated notation.",
                "source": "MIM curation (#321)"
              },
              {
                "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
                "notes": "mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning* than CHEBI:34683 ('disodium hydrogenphosphate') — a subsumption ChEBI itself denies: it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 'hydrate', never under the anhydrous compound, which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record's own identifier are unchanged.",
                "source": "MIM curation (#342)"
              },
              {
                "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
                "notes": "NCI EVS NCIt 26.10d NCIT:C61946 'Sodium Phosphate, Dibasic, Heptahydrate' is active and explicitly records CAS 7782-85-6, formula 2Na.HO4P.7H2O and FDA UNII 70WT22SF4B. Source: https://api-evsrest.nci.nih.gov/api/v1/concept/ncit/C61946?include=full; accessed 2026-11-01; archived at reports/ncit_heptahydrate_875_20261101/sources/ncit-C61946.json (sha256 a112c3e91dd6aa46feb112621ba5d13673df69f1b20665e042e22b8aa05a1d83). The approved #875 decision uses MAPPING_SEMANTICS section 3 step 1, which precedes the CAS fallback. The anhydrous CHEBI:34683 is not this identity.",
                "source": "https://api-evsrest.nci.nih.gov/api/v1/concept/ncit/C61946?include=full"
              }
            ],
            "mapping_quality": "EXACT_MATCH",
            "ontology_id": "NCIT:C61946",
            "ontology_label": "Sodium Phosphate, Dibasic, Heptahydrate",
            "ontology_source": "NCIT"
          },
          "path": "data/ingredients/mapped/Na2hpo4_X_7_H2o.yaml",
          "preferred_term": "Na2HPO4 x 7 H2O",
