                "notes": "[HISTORICAL — superseded by the #321 re-grade below: this record is a hydrate of CHEBI:37585, not an exact match to it] Imported from CultureMech pipeline, quality=DIRECT_MATCH",
                "source": "CultureMech"
              },
              {
                "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
                "notes": "identifier CHEBI:37585 -> kgmicrobe.compound:nah2po4_x_2_h2o; mapping_quality SYNONYM_MATCH -> NARROW_MATCH. The record is a hydrate of CHEBI:37585 ('sodium dihydrogenphosphate') and was sharing that term's identifier — the identity collapse MAPPING_SEMANTICS §3 forbids, which made a distinct substance indistinguishable from its anhydrous parent downstream. ChEBI has no term for this hydrate and the record carries no verified CAS, so steps 1 and 2 are unavailable and step 3 applies.",
                "source": "MIM curation (#321/#334)"
              },
              {
                "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
                "notes": "molecular_formula 'H2O4P.Na' -> 'H2O4P.Na.2H2O'. The recorded value described the anhydrous salt while the label names a hydrate, understating the mass by 18 g/mol per water. Corrected because the label states 2 water(s) of hydration, and the recorded formula was byte-identical to the anhydrous parent CHEBI:37585's ChEBI formula ('H2O4P.Na') — the mark of a value inherited from the parent rather than measured for this record. Water appended in ChEBI's own dot-separated notation.",
                "source": "MIM curation (#321)"
              },
              {
                "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
                "notes": "mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning* than CHEBI:37585 ('sodium dihydrogenphosphate') — a subsumption ChEBI itself denies: it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 'hydrate', never under the anhydrous compound, which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record's own identifier are unchanged.",
                "source": "MIM curation (#342)"
              }
            ],
