              {
                "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
                "notes": "identifier CHEBI:35696 -> kgmicrobe.compound:cocl2_x_2_h2o; mapping_quality EXACT_MATCH -> NARROW_MATCH. The record is a hydrate of CHEBI:35696 ('cobalt dichloride') and was sharing that term's identifier — the identity collapse MAPPING_SEMANTICS §3 forbids, which made a distinct substance indistinguishable from its anhydrous parent downstream. ChEBI has no term for this hydrate and the record carries no verified CAS, so steps 1 and 2 are unavailable and step 3 applies.",
